## Complete structural inspection

The lexer processes the entire dump with quote escaping, doubled quotes, comments, custom DELIMITER directives and multiline INSERT handling. It identifies CREATE DATABASE ignition_config, USE ignition_config, one CREATE TABLE alarm_event_data, 57 INSERT starts (56 terminated and one pending), and zero standalone routine/trigger/event definitions. The last INSERT begins at line 1333906, spans 994866 text characters, and ends at EOF with a comma (character code 44), requiring another VALUES tuple. Quotes and parentheses are balanced at EOF, so this is a missing continuation, not a quote-parser failure. The completion marker and closing session restoration/unlock statements are absent.

Absence of a semicolon or completion comment alone would not establish a defective export: clients can accept some final statements at EOF, and comments can be disabled. Here the dangling comma plus the independent database-engine failure are decisive.

## Isolated MariaDB 10.11 validation

The installed 10.11.11 binaries initialized a disposable restricted datadir. This did not install/reinstall software or register a service. The test server used a unique authenticated named pipe, skip_networking=1, event_scheduler=OFF, disabled replication startup/binlogging and local infile, and a restricted file directory. No TCP listener or destination database was used.

The unchanged original SQL was streamed as binary client stdin. The client returned exit code 1, **ERROR 1064 / SQLSTATE 42000 at line 1333906**. No confidential error excerpt or records were logged. Partial-test inventory: one table alarm_event_data, 1,333,799 successfully inserted rows, zero routines, zero triggers and zero events. These are disposable partial-import counts, not recovered destination data or a full source count. The disposable server was stopped. Both existing Windows services remained running and untouched.

## Parser corrections and restoration safeguards

Analyze-Staging.ps1 now uses SqlStructure.cs instead of line regex for SQL object/statement classification. Regression fixtures cover large/multiline INSERT structure, escaped and doubled quotes, semicolons inside values, custom routine delimiters, EOF comments, incomplete rows, unclosed quotes and embedded routine SQL inside a stored data record.

The earlier system-dump regex could count names/SQL inside mysql.proc/mysql.event INSERT records as standalone CREATE routines/events. Corrected counts are 31 CREATE TABLE statements and zero standalone CREATE PROCEDURE/FUNCTION/EVENT statements. Stored system-table records still require careful selective review. The global mysql dump is not a safe replacement for a complete contextual export. Existing live-restore safety gates remain in force; missing records were not invented and the partial import was not promoted.

